      "writtenOn": "2019-08-05T18:20:54Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Is there a follow-up patch to this? If not, then how can the heaps use their own dmabuf operations?\n\nIf there is a subsequent patch, will it be possible to forego the use of the ion_dma_buf_ops structure (i.e. the buffer provides its own dma_buf_ops pointer), or is it the approach you discussed where you will add an extra field in the heaps to provide dma buf operations, and you\u0027ll still export the buffer in ion.c with ion_dma_buf_ops, but the ion_dma_buf_ops will check first to see if the heap has implemented the op in question, and use that implementation, otherwise, use the generic one?",
      "revId": "8d94fc8385460d1f1074f9e5352b154c967b371c",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "110a9b58_95052548",
        "filename": "drivers/staging/android/ion/ion.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 184,
      "author": {
        "id": 1108565
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-08-05T19:13:04Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yes, which is what the big complain from Greg was. So, I am now splitting the whole series.\n\nTo answer your question, yeah, I think the later works better for us too. There is a new user of libion in Android system image as well :( (IIRC, you had no objections either way, correct?).",
      "parentUuid": "06880035_f016c70a",
      "revId": "8d94fc8385460d1f1074f9e5352b154c967b371c",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "f8bb421a_2556d4dc",
        "filename": "drivers/staging/android/ion/ion.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 184,
      "author": {
        "id": 1530208
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-08-05T19:37:20Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Okay.\n\nWas the rationale for having the latter model so that it is easier for you to track memory usage and do cache maintenance profiling? If so, why not just use traces in the dma-buf layer, or would that be overkill since there may be other exporters at some point, and you\u0027re only really worried about capturing stats on ION memory?\n\nAlso, can you please elaborate on this new user of libion in the system image? How does that impact this? Is it because they expect a dma-buf fd, so the core needs to export it? Why can\u0027t the heaps do it?",
      "parentUuid": "110a9b58_95052548",
      "revId": "8d94fc8385460d1f1074f9e5352b154c967b371c",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
