        "id": 1530208
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-08-05T18:20:54Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Out of curiosity, what was the rationale for exposing the ION internals to the rest of the kernel? Do they need to know about all this stuff?",
      "revId": "8d94fc8385460d1f1074f9e5352b154c967b371c",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "dce6e78b_6be8a1d9",
        "filename": "include/linux/ion.h",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 50,
      "author": {
        "id": 1108565
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-08-05T19:13:04Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "So, the ion_heap is needed by the \"rest\" (heap drivers). The ion_heap_type is needed by the allocators. So, I guess we can move the ion_device and the ion_buffer back into staging and call the file ion_private.h or something.\nAs things stood, it was randomly hidden, so I just went ahead and opened up everything. We can find a good middle ground like you said.\n\n(I also don\u0027t like the fact that ion_device represents a \"subsystem\", but I guess that\u0027s getting fixed with the dmabuf based heaps anyway)",
      "parentUuid": "ae938134_4273d753",
      "revId": "8d94fc8385460d1f1074f9e5352b154c967b371c",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "9aac104d_bc761018",
        "filename": "include/linux/ion.h",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 50,
      "author": {
        "id": 1530208
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-08-05T19:37:20Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yes. It\u0027s not really a big deal. I just wanted to see if there\u0027s something else going on that would require the rest of the kernel--besides the heaps, and ION of course--to know what an ION heap is.",
      "parentUuid": "dce6e78b_6be8a1d9",
      "revId": "8d94fc8385460d1f1074f9e5352b154c967b371c",
